WEBVTT

14
00:01:25.124 --> 00:01:26.687
Jamie · Customer: Hi, this is Jamie.

15
00:01:28.473 --> 00:01:37.913
Emily · Agent: Hi Jamie, this is Emily Carter from the Holcim Sales team, you made an enquiry on our website earlier about a project you're currently working on.

16
00:01:38.174 --> 00:01:48.459
Jamie · Customer: Hi Emily. Yea, I need 250 tonnes of MOT Type 1 aggregate dropped at a new logistics yard near Rugby. Just need it to prep the hardstanding.

17
00:01:49.749 --> 00:02:04.029
Emily · Agent: I can get that sorted for you. 250 tonnes to Rugby. While I put that through, are you laying standard tarmac over the top, or have you got specific drainage requirements for this site?

18
00:02:05.004 --> 00:02:17.534
Jamie · Customer: The council is breathing down our necks about surface water runoff, to be honest. We need some sort of sustainable drainage for the car park, plus a really heavy-duty slab for the lorry loading bays.

19
00:02:22.736 --> 00:02:36.816
Emily · Agent: Right, for the drainage, you'll want to look at our SuperDrain Asphalt. It's a permeable surface, so the water drains straight through it into the sub-base. It keeps the council happy and saves digging extra drainage channels.

20
00:02:37.074 --> 00:02:40.397
Jamie · Customer: Never used that before. Does it actually work?

21
00:02:41.629 --> 00:02:54.869
Emily · Agent: It does, it's fully SuDS compliant. And for the lorry bays, we can supply a steel fibre-reinforced concrete. You won't even need to lay steel mesh, which will save your lads a lot of time on site.

22
00:02:55.834 --> 00:03:02.726
Jamie · Customer: Sounds spot on. Get your technical bloke to give me a ring about that slab pour, and send the prices over for the rest.

